abstract: >-
  A fixed-reference common-action benchmark for one-loop stress and paired
  scalar sources of a free massive minimally coupled scalar in the Euclidean
  de Sitter state. Four registered points are checked by spectral and separate
  proper-time implementations, with an exact energy, pressure and variance
  mode check at one curved point. A separately resolved classical shell
  susceptibility supplies local source-response coefficients. This work does
  not select physical masses or gravitational matching, solve quantum-corrected
  backreaction, derive a causal evolution kernel, or establish heating. Internal
  AI-assisted cross-checks are not external peer review. Text and data use
  CC BY 4.0; source code uses MIT.
